# =============================================================================
# Reusable .gitignore for Python projects
# Version: 1.0.0   Created: 2026-11-11   Updated: 2026-11-11
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing below names this project. Copy the file unchanged into any repo.
# Conventions it relies on:
#   - Private, never-commit folders start with "_private" (e.g. _private_transcripts/)
#   - Generated output goes in logs/, output/, or a folder ending in "_results"
# Pattern notes:
#   - "name/" (trailing slash only) matches that folder at ANY depth, with
#     everything inside it, including subfolders and dot-files.
#   - A slash elsewhere ("a/b") anchors the pattern to this file's folder only.
#   - .gitignore only affects untracked files, and `git add -f` overrides it.
# =============================================================================

# --- Private material: never commit ----------------------------------------
*_private*/
*transcript*

# --- Secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
credentials.json
# *credentials*.*   # exclude code files like "credentials_check.py"
client_secret*.json
token.json
*.pem
*.key


# --- Generated output ------------------------------------------------------
logs/
output/
*_results/

# --- Python ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- OS / editor -----------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
